# Kafka Setup Guide (KRaft Mode) – From UID Creation to Topic Creation

This document explains how to set up **Apache Kafka in KRaft mode (without Zookeeper)** and create a topic for use with Spring Boot microservices.

---

# 1. Generate Kafka Cluster ID (UID)

Open a terminal and navigate to the Kafka installation directory.

```bash
cd C:\kafka
```

Generate a new Cluster ID:

```bash
.\bin\windows\kafka-storage.bat random-uuid
```

Example output:

```
m5HBz1CxR4GKy2LQppaTsA
```

Copy this value. It will be used in the next step.

---

# 2. Format Kafka Storage

Kafka must format the metadata directory before starting the broker.

Run the following command using the generated UID:

```bash
.\bin\windows\kafka-storage.bat format -t rWvVSXc8ROuPQZVXLalVQg -c .\config\server.properties
```

Expected output:

```
Formatting metadata directory C:/kafka/kraft-logs with metadata.version 4.0-IV3
```

This initializes Kafka storage.

---

# 3. Start Kafka Broker

Start the Kafka server using the server configuration file.

```bash
.\bin\windows\kafka-server-start.bat .\config\server.properties
```

Kafka will start and listen on:

```
localhost:9092
```

Keep this terminal running.

---

# 4. Create a Kafka Topic

Open a **new terminal** and run:

```bash
.\bin\windows\kafka-topics.bat --create --topic silver-to-gold-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --partitions 1 --replication-factor 1
```

Expected output:

```
Created topic silver-to-gold-topic
```

---

# 5. Verify Topic Creation

List all topics:

```bash
.\bin\windows\kafka-topics.bat --list --bootstrap-server localhost:9092
```

Example output:

```
silver-to-gold-topic
```

---

# 6. Describe Topic

To view topic details:

```bash
.\bin\windows\kafka-topics.bat --describe --topic silver-to-gold-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092
```

Example output:

```
Topic: silver-to-gold-topic
PartitionCount: 1
ReplicationFactor: 1
Leader: 1
```

---

# 7. Test Kafka Producer (Optional)

Run a console producer:

```bash
.\bin\windows\kafka-console-producer.bat --topic silver-to-gold-topic --bootstrap-server localhost:9092
```

Type a message:

```
hello
```

---

# 8. Test Kafka Consumer

Run a console consumer to read messages:

```bash
.\bin\windows\kafka-console-consumer.bat --topic silver-to-gold-topic --from-beginning --bootstrap-server localhost:9092
```

Example output:

```
hello
```

---

# 9. Use Topic in Spring Boot

In your Spring Boot service, send messages using:

```java
kafkaTemplate.send("silver-to-gold-topic", silverProcessedResponseBody);
```

Ensure the topic exists before running the application.

---

# Kafka Setup Workflow

```
1. Generate Cluster UID
2. Format Kafka storage
3. Start Kafka broker
4. Create topic
5. Verify topic
6. Run Spring Boot services
```

---

# Example Microservice Data Flow

```
Bronze Service
     ↓
Kafka Topic (bronze-topic)
     ↓
Silver Service
     ↓
Kafka Topic (silver-topic)
     ↓
Gold Service
```

This setup supports a typical **data enrichment pipeline architecture** using Kafka.
